  "published": "2026-11-13T19:09:00.227Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "v0.7.0: C# 15 union outcomes, net11.0 only. IBillingWebhookProcessor.ProcessWebhookAsync returns a WebhookOutcome and IExternalPurchaseClaims.ClaimHeldAsync returns a ClaimOutcome, so a host can switch over what happened instead of reading a bool. Both are registered by AddTechTeaStudioBilling and run the same code as HandleWebhookAsync and ClaimAsync, which stay on every target. Older targets are unchanged.\n\nv0.6.1: Adds the net11.0 target. No API or behaviour change.\n\nv0.6.0: Payment hardening: strict YooKassa webhook ids, refund events on every provider through the optional IBillingRefundFulfillment, Telegram pre-checkout declines stale invoices and failed payments are redelivered, Stripe Mode defaults to payment. BREAKING: ITelegramBot.AnswerPreCheckoutAsync takes payload, amount and currency.\n\nv0.5.3: TelegramStarsBillingProvider can mint invoice LINKS (Bot API createInvoiceLink) via ITelegramBot.CreateInvoiceLinkAsync - the payment sheet opens directly, no bot chat and no /start. The deep-link flow only shows START to a user who never started the bot; a returning user got a silent chat and no invoice.\n\nv0.5.0: TechTeaStudio.Billing.Abstractions additionally targets netstandard2.0 and net472, so .NET Framework 4.6.2+ assemblies can share the contracts. This package itself stays .NET 5+ - it needs the ASP.NET Core shared framework, which has not run on .NET Framework since ASP.NET Core 3.0.\n\nv0.4.0: Targets net5.0 through net10.0 (was net8.0+). Contracts split into the dependency-free TechTeaStudio.Billing.Abstractions package, pulled in automatically - namespaces are unchanged, so existing code compiles as-is. Webhook endpoints now map through RequestDelegate instead of minimal-API lambdas, which is what makes net5.0/net6.0 possible; behaviour and status codes are identical. Symbol packages, SourceLink and package validation added.\n\nFull changelog: https://github.com/TechTeaStudio/Billing/blob/product/CHANGELOG.md",
